IMPORT prelude

-- Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- the start-up concession for employee share schemes (ss 83A-25,
-- 83A-33, 83A-45), the R&D tax offset rate (s 355-100) and the early stage investor tax offset (ss 360-15, 360-20, 360-25).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 267, compilation date 27 August 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 79, 2026; register id
-- C2026C00400, 12 volumes), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A05138.txt.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0001 in subjects/au/requirements.jsonl (priority 1): raised 24 times by the three Western
-- Australian cradle-to-grave lives. This module answers chloe c072 and daniel d04b (start-up ESS interests at Jarrah Legal
-- Technologies, 2034), daniel d049 (the R&D tax incentive, 2032) and daniel d081 (angel investments as a sophisticated
-- investor, 2056). SCOPED to those questions.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The deferred-taxing route (Subdiv 83A-C) and the CGT treatment of ESS interests (Subdiv 130-D); the "other cases"
-- reduction (s 83A-35); the broad-availability condition (s 83A-105(2)) is a single input; what an R&D entity, R&D activity or
-- notional deduction is (Div 355 generally), the $150 million ceiling, and the R&D premium for larger entities (s 355-100(1A));
-- the corporate tax rate, which comes from the Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (an INPUT); the early stage innovation company test
-- (s 360-40, its 100-point test in s 360-45) beyond one input; the modified CGT treatment for ESIC shares (Subdiv 360-B);
-- carry-forward of the offset. Aggregated turnover (s 328-115) is an input throughout.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT FOR PUBLIC USE. See NOTES.md.

§ `Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 -- business and investment`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `83A-25, 83A-33, 83A-45 -- employee share schemes: the start-up concession`

-- s 83A-25(1): "Your assessable income for the income year in which you acquire the *ESS interest includes the discount".
-- s 83A-33(1): reduce that amount by the amounts for ESS interests to which subsections (2) to (6), s 83A-45 and (for shares)
-- s 83A-105(2) all apply:
--   (2) no equity interests in the company or its group "listed for quotation in the official list of any *approved stock
--       exchange";
--   (3) the company and the others "incorporated ... less than 10 years before the end of the first company's most recent income
--       year before you acquired the interest";
--   (4) "an *aggregated turnover not exceeding $50 million for the company's most recent income year";
--   (5) for a share, "the discount on the ESS interest is no more than 15% of its *market value when you acquire it"; for a
--       right, "the amount that must be paid to exercise the right is greater than or equal to the market value of an ordinary
--       share";
--   (6) "your employer is an Australian resident".
-- s 83A-45: (1) employed by the company or a subsidiary; (2) the scheme relates only to ordinary shares; (3) not a share-trading
-- company integrity case; (4)-(5) a minimum holding period of 3 years (or until employment ends) during which disposal is not
-- permitted; (6) "you do not hold a beneficial interest in more than 10% of the *shares" nor control more than 10% of the votes.
DECLARE EssInterest HAS
    `is a right rather than a share` IS A BOOLEAN
    `discount` IS A NUMBER
    `market value` IS A NUMBER
    `exercise price` IS A NUMBER
    `group has listed equity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years incorporated before the last income year end` IS A NUMBER
    `aggregated turnover last year` IS A NUMBER
    `employer is an Australian resident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed by the company or a subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `scheme relates only to ordinary shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `share trading company integrity case` IS A BOOLEAN
    `three-year disposal restriction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds more than 10 percent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `scheme broadly available` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the interest` IS AN EssInterest
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the market value condition is met` IF
    IF `the interest`'s `is a right rather than a share`
    THEN `the interest`'s `exercise price` AT LEAST `the interest`'s `market value`
    ELSE `the interest`'s `discount` TIMES 100 AT MOST `the interest`'s `market value` TIMES 15

GIVEN `the interest` IS AN EssInterest
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the start-up concession applies` IF
        (NOT `the interest`'s `group has listed equity`)
    AND `the interest`'s `years incorporated before the last income year end` LESS THAN 10
    AND `the interest`'s `aggregated turnover last year` AT MOST 50000000
    AND `the market value condition is met` `the interest`
    AND `the interest`'s `employer is an Australian resident`
    AND `the interest`'s `employed by the company or a subsidiary`
    AND `the interest`'s `scheme relates only to ordinary shares`
    AND (NOT `the interest`'s `share trading company integrity case`)
    AND `the interest`'s `three-year disposal restriction`
    AND (NOT `the interest`'s `holds more than 10 percent`)
    AND (`the interest`'s `is a right rather than a share` OR `the interest`'s `scheme broadly available`)

-- The amount left in assessable income under s 83A-25 after the s 83A-33 reduction.
GIVEN `the interest` IS AN EssInterest
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ESS discount assessable` MEANS
    IF `the start-up concession applies` `the interest` THEN 0 ELSE `the interest`'s `discount`

§§ `355-100 -- R&D tax offset`

-- s 355-100(1), notional deductions between $20,000 and $150 million. Table item 1: "the *R&D entity's *aggregated turnover for
-- the income year is less than $20 million (and item 2 of this table does not apply)" -- "the R&D entity's *corporate tax rate for
-- the income year, plus 18.5 percentage points". Item 2 (controlled by exempt entities) and item 3 ("any other case") -- "the
-- R&D entity's *corporate tax rate", increased by the premium in (1A) (not encoded). Note 1: "The tax offset will be a
-- refundable tax offset if item 1 of the table applies (see section 67-30)."
-- s 355-100(2): if the notional deductions are less than $20,000, only expenditure to a registered research service provider
-- and CRC contributions count (collapsed to one input).
GIVEN `aggregated turnover` IS A NUMBER, `controlled by exempt entities` IS A BOOLEAN, `corporate tax rate in percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the R&D offset rate in percent before any premium` MEANS
    IF `aggregated turnover` LESS THAN 20000000 AND NOT `controlled by exempt entities`
    THEN `corporate tax rate in percent` PLUS 185 DIVIDED BY 10
    ELSE `corporate tax rate in percent`

GIVEN `aggregated turnover` IS A NUMBER, `controlled by exempt entities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the R&D offset is refundable` IF
    `aggregated turnover` LESS THAN 20000000 AND NOT `controlled by exempt entities`

GIVEN `notional deductions` IS A NUMBER, `research service provider and CRC expenditure` IS A NUMBER,
      `aggregated turnover` IS A NUMBER, `corporate tax rate in percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the small company's refundable R&D offset` MEANS
    (IF `notional deductions` LESS THAN 20000 THEN `research service provider and CRC expenditure` ELSE `notional deductions`)
    TIMES `the R&D offset rate in percent before any premium` `aggregated turnover` FALSE `corporate tax rate in percent`
    DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `360-15, 360-20, 360-25 -- early stage investor tax offset`

-- s 360-15(1): entitled if not a trust, partnership, ESVCLP or widely held company; a company issues you shares; s 360-40(1)
-- (early stage innovation company) applies immediately after; not affiliates; not ESS interests; and immediately after the issue
-- you do not hold more than 30% of income, capital or voting rights.
-- s 360-20(1): no entitlement if none of "subsections 708(8), (10) or (11) of the Corporations Act 2001 removed the need for a
-- disclosure document" and "a total of more than $50,000 was paid" for the shares in the income year.
-- s 360-25(1): "20% of the sum" of money and non-cash benefits received for the issue; (2) reduced so that the offsets for the
-- year and those carried forward, for you and your affiliates, do "not exceed $200,000".
GIVEN `eligible investor and company` IS A BOOLEAN, `sophisticated or professional investor` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `amount paid in the year` IS A NUMBER, `offsets already counted toward the cap` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the early stage investor tax offset` MEANS
    IF (NOT `eligible investor and company`) OR ((NOT `sophisticated or professional investor`) AND `amount paid in the year` GREATER THAN 50000)
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the lesser of` (`amount paid in the year` TIMES 20 DIVIDED BY 100)
                         (`the greater of` (200000 MINUS `offsets already counted toward the cap`) 0)
